{"1-8":{"people":[{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":7,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":4,"firstVerse":2}],"places":[{"id":"moriah-mount-h4179","name":"Moriah Mount","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":2}],"words":[{"base":"H0085","lemma":"אַבְרָהָם","tr":"av·ra·ham","gloss":"Abraham","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":175},{"base":"H5930","lemma":"עֹלָה","tr":"o·lah","gloss":"burnt offering","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":287},{"base":"H3327","lemma":"יִצְחָק","tr":"yits·chaq","gloss":"Isaac","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":108},{"base":"H5288","lemma":"נַ֫עַר","tr":"na·ar","gloss":"youth","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":239},{"base":"H3947","lemma":"לָקַח","tr":"la·qach","gloss":"to take: take","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":966},{"base":"H6086","lemma":"עֵץ","tr":"ets","gloss":"tree: wood","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":330},{"base":"H7716","lemma":"שֶׂה","tr":"seh","gloss":"sheep","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":47},{"base":"H8147","lemma":"שְׁנַ֫יִם","tr":"she·na·yim","gloss":"two","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":768},{"base":"H2543","lemma":"חֲמוֹר","tr":"cha·mor","gloss":"donkey","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":96},{"base":"H2009","lemma":"הִנֵּה","tr":"hin·neh","gloss":"behold","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":843}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JHN","chapter":3,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":34,"source":"both","text":"For God so loved the world that He gave His one and only Son, that everyone who believes in Him shall not perish but have eternal life.","from":2},{"book":"HEB","chapter":11,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":28,"source":"both","text":"By faith Abraham, when he was tested, offered up Isaac on the altar. He who had received the promises was ready to offer his one and only son,","from":1},{"book":"ROM","chapter":8,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":26,"source":"both","text":"He who did not spare His own Son but gave Him up for us all, how will He not also, along with Him, freely give us all things?","from":2},{"book":"DEU","chapter":8,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"Remember that these forty years the LORD your God led you all the way in the wilderness, so that He might humble you and test you in order to know what was in your heart, whether or not you would keep His commandments.","from":1},{"book":"JAS","chapter":1,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"Blessed is the man who perseveres under trial, because when he has stood the test, he will receive the crown of life that God has promised to those who love Him.","from":1},{"book":"JAS","chapter":1,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"But each one is tempted when by his own evil desires he is lured away and enticed.","from":1},{"book":"JAS","chapter":2,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"Was not our father Abraham justified by what he did when he offered his son Isaac on the altar?","from":1},{"book":"1PE","chapter":1,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"so that the proven character of your faith—more precious than gold, which perishes even though refined by fire—may result in praise, glory, and honor at the revelation of Jesus Christ.","from":1}],"notes":[{"id":"gen-22-isaac-bound","title":"The binding of Isaac","kind":"type"}],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"9-14":{"people":[{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":5,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":1,"firstVerse":9}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0085","lemma":"אַבְרָהָם","tr":"av·ra·ham","gloss":"Abraham","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":175},{"base":"H0352","lemma":"אַ֫יִל","tr":"a·yil","gloss":"ram","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":187},{"base":"H6086","lemma":"עֵץ","tr":"ets","gloss":"tree: wood","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":330},{"base":"H4196","lemma":"מִזְבֵּחַ","tr":"miz·be·ach","gloss":"altar","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":401},{"base":"H4725","lemma":"מָקוֹם","tr":"ma·qom","gloss":"place","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":401},{"base":"H3979","lemma":"מַאֲכֶ֫לֶת","tr":"ma·a·khe·let","gloss":"knife","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H5442","lemma":"סְבַךְ","tr":"se·vakh","gloss":"thicket","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H0408","lemma":"אַל","tr":"al","gloss":"not","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":724},{"base":"H7121","lemma":"קָרָא","tr":"qa·ra","gloss":"to call: call to","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":733},{"base":"H2009","lemma":"הִנֵּה","tr":"hin·neh","gloss":"behold","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":843}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JAS","chapter":2,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":26,"source":"openbible","text":"Was not our father Abraham justified by what he did when he offered his son Isaac on the altar?","from":12},{"book":"JAS","chapter":2,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":26,"source":"openbible","text":"You see that his faith was working with his actions, and his faith was perfected by what he did.","from":12},{"book":"EXO","chapter":17,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"And Moses built an altar and named it The LORD Is My Banner.","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":22,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"Abraham answered, “God Himself will provide the lamb for the burnt offering, my son.” And the two walked on together.","from":14},{"book":"JDG","chapter":6,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"So Gideon built an altar to the LORD there and called it The LORD Is Peace. To this day it stands in Ophrah of the Abiezrites.","from":14},{"book":"JAS","chapter":2,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"But someone will say, “You have faith and I have deeds.” Show me your faith without deeds, and I will show you my faith by my deeds.","from":12},{"book":"1SA","chapter":15,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"But Samuel declared: “Does the LORD delight in burnt offerings and sacrifices as much as in obedience to His voice? Behold, obedience is better than sacrifice, and attentiveness is better than the fat of rams.","from":12},{"book":"ROM","chapter":8,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"He who did not spare His own Son but gave Him up for us all, how will He not also, along with Him, freely give us all things?","from":12}],"notes":[{"id":"gen-22-isaac-bound","title":"The binding of Isaac","kind":"type"}],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"15-19":{"people":[{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":2,"firstVerse":15}],"places":[{"id":"beersheba-h0884","name":"Beersheba","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":19}],"words":[{"base":"H0884","lemma":"בְּאֵר שֶׁ֫בַע","tr":"be·er she·va","gloss":"Beersheba","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":68},{"base":"H0085","lemma":"אַבְרָהָם","tr":"av·ra·ham","gloss":"Abraham","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":175},{"base":"H2233","lemma":"זֶ֫רַע","tr":"ze·ra","gloss":"seed","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":229},{"base":"H1288","lemma":"בָּרַךְ","tr":"ba·rakh","gloss":"to bless","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":330},{"base":"H7235","lemma":"רָבָה","tr":"ra·vah","gloss":"to multiply","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":227},{"base":"H8064","lemma":"שָׁמַיִם","tr":"sha·ma·yim","gloss":"heaven","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":421},{"base":"H3173","lemma":"יָחִיד","tr":"ya·chid","gloss":"only","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H6118","lemma":"עֵ֫קֶב","tr":"e·qev","gloss":"consequence","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":15},{"base":"H2344","lemma":"חוֹל","tr":"chol","gloss":"sand","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":23},{"base":"H2820","lemma":"חָשַׂךְ","tr":"cha·sakh","gloss":"to withhold","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":28}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":3,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":24,"source":"both","text":"And you are sons of the prophets and of the covenant God made with your fathers when He said to Abraham, ‘Through your offspring all the families of the earth will be blessed.’","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"I will bless those who bless you and curse those who curse you; and all the families of the earth will be blessed through you.”","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":15,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"And the Lordtook him outside and said, “Now look to the heavens and count the stars, if you are able.” Then He told him, “So shall your offspring be.”","from":17},{"book":"GEN","chapter":26,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"I will make your descendants as numerous as the stars in the sky, and I will give them all these lands, and through your offspring all nations of the earth will be blessed,","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":26,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"because Abraham listened to My voice and kept My charge, My commandments, My statutes, and My laws.”","from":18},{"book":"GAL","chapter":3,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"The promises were spoken to Abraham and to his seed. The Scripture does not say, “and to seeds,” meaning many, but “and to your seed,” meaning One, who is Christ.","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":13,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"I will make your offspring like the dust of the earth, so that if one could count the dust of the earth, then your offspring could be counted.","from":17},{"book":"JER","chapter":33,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"As the hosts of heaven cannot be counted and as the sand on the seashore cannot be measured, so too will I multiply the descendants of My servant David and the Levites who minister before Me.”","from":17}],"notes":[{"id":"gen-12-3","title":"All nations blessed through Abraham","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[]},"20-24":{"people":[{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":2,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"milcah-h4435g","name":"Milcah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Lot","count":2,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"nahor-h5152h","name":"Nahor","kind":"person","brief":"Abraham's brother","count":2,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"aram-h0758h","name":"Aram","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Kemuel","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"buz-h0938g","name":"Buz","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"kemuel-h7055g","name":"Kemuel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"uz-h5780h","name":"Uz","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"bethuel-h1328a","name":"Bethuel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"chesed-h3777","name":"Chesed","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"hazo-h2375","name":"Hazo","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"jidlaph-h3044","name":"Jidlaph","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"pildash-h6394","name":"Pildash","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"rebekah-h7259","name":"Rebekah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Laban","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"gaham-h1514","name":"Gaham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"maacah-h4601g","name":"Maacah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"reumah-h7208","name":"Reumah","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"tahash-h8477","name":"Tahash","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"tebah-h2875","name":"Tebah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":1,"firstVerse":24}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","tr":"ya·lad","gloss":"to beget","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":496},{"base":"H1328","lemma":"בְּתוּאֵל","tr":"be·tu·el","gloss":"Bethuel","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":10},{"base":"H4435","lemma":"מִלְכָּה","tr":"mil·kah","gloss":"Milcah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H5152","lemma":"נָחוֹר","tr":"na·chor","gloss":"Nahor","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":18},{"base":"H0251","lemma":"אָח","tr":"ach","gloss":"brother: male-sibling","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":629},{"base":"H0085","lemma":"אַבְרָהָם","tr":"av·ra·ham","gloss":"Abraham","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":175},{"base":"H0938","lemma":"בּוּז","tr":"buz","gloss":"Buz","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H7055","lemma":"קְמוּאֵל","tr":"qe·mu·el","gloss":"Kemuel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H5780","lemma":"עוּץ","tr":"uts","gloss":"Uz","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H0428","lemma":"אֵ֫לֶּה","tr":"el·leh","gloss":"these","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":746}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":11,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And Abram and Nahor took wives for themselves. Abramʼs wife was named Sarai, and Nahorʼs wife was named Milcah; she was the daughter of Haran, who was the father of both Milcah and Iscah.","from":20},{"book":"GEN","chapter":24,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Before the servant had finished praying, Rebekah came out with her jar on her shoulder. She was the daughter of Bethuel son of Milcah, the wife of Abrahamʼs brother Nahor.","from":23},{"book":"GEN","chapter":11,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Terah was 70 years old, he became the father of Abram, Nahor, and Haran.","from":20},{"book":"GEN","chapter":16,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So after he had lived in Canaan for ten years, his wife Sarai took her Egyptian maidservant Hagar and gave her to Abram to be his wife.","from":24},{"book":"GEN","chapter":24,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the servant took ten of his masterʼs camels and departed with all manner of good things from his master in hand. And he set out for Nahorʼs hometown in Aram-naharaim.","from":20},{"book":"GEN","chapter":24,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the servant took ten of his masterʼs camels and departed with all manner of good things from his master in hand. And he set out for Nahorʼs hometown in Aram-naharaim.","from":21},{"book":"GEN","chapter":24,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Before the servant had finished praying, Rebekah came out with her jar on her shoulder. She was the daughter of Bethuel son of Milcah, the wife of Abrahamʼs brother Nahor.","from":20},{"book":"GEN","chapter":24,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"She replied, “I am the daughter of Bethuel, the son that Milcah bore to Nahor.”","from":20}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}